.TH "KOSH" "1" "" "kosh" "Koshka Manual"
.SH NAME
kosh \- declarative and operational specification for the Koshka command
shell, static analyzer, formatter, language server, interactive line
editor, and bundled Koshkit utilities across Linux, macOS, and
Windows[cite: 4]
.PP
2026\-10\-26[cite: 4]
.PP
Prerequisites \- Familiarity with POSIX shell fundamentals and kosh(5)
configuration settings[cite: 4].
.PP
\f[CR]kosh\f[R] is the Koshka command shell[cite: 4].
The binary integrates a POSIX and Bash\-compatible command interpreter,
a pre\-execution static analyzer, a source code formatter, a Language
Server Protocol (LSP) daemon, and the \f[CR]koshkit\f[R] suite of
bundled POSIX and system utilities[cite: 4].
Identical parser grammar and execution semantics operate across Linux,
macOS, and Windows[cite: 4].
.SH CORE SYSTEM PRIMITIVES
.PP
.TS
