.TE
.SS Prompt rendering and escape sequences
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Prompt lifecycle\f[R] \- Before reading interactive input, the
shell executes \f[CR]PROMPT_COMMAND\f[R] (a single command or an indexed
array of commands executed sequentially, preserving the prior
command\[aq]s \f[CR]$?\f[R] and \f[CR]$_\f[R]) and prints \f[CR]PS1\f[R]
and the right prompt (\f[CR]RPS1\f[R], or \f[CR]RPROMPT\f[R] if
\f[CR]RPS1\f[R] is unset/empty, defaulting to dim
\f[CR]\[rs]L \[rs]M\f[R])[cite: 4].
After reading input and before execution, \f[CR]PS0\f[R] prints[cite:
4].
\f[CR]PS2\f[R] defaults to \f[CR]> \f[R] (unused by the interactive
editor, which submits full multi\-line buffers on \f[CR]Enter\f[R]),
\f[CR]PS3\f[R] prompts for \f[CR]select\f[R] (\f[CR]#? \f[R] default),
and \f[CR]PS4\f[R] prefixes \f[CR]xtrace\f[R] lines (\f[CR]+ \f[R]
default, repeating its first byte per nesting level of substitution,
\f[CR]eval\f[R], \f[CR]source\f[R], or trap)[cite: 4].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Expansion and transient prompts\f[R] \- \f[CR]PS0\f[R],
\f[CR]PS1\f[R], \f[CR]PS2\f[R], and \f[CR]RPS1\f[R]/\f[CR]RPROMPT\f[R]
process backslash escapes first, then undergo parameter, command, and
arithmetic expansion (\f[CR]PS4\f[R] prints literally)[cite: 4].
Setting non\-empty \f[CR]KOSH_TRANSIENT_PS1\f[R] or
\f[CR]KOSH_TRANSIENT_RPS1\f[R] replaces \f[CR]PS1\f[R] and
\f[CR]RPS1\f[R] in scrollback upon \f[CR]Enter\f[R] or
\f[CR]Ctrl\-C\f[R] (\f[CR]KOSH_TRANSIENT_RPS1\f[R] defaults to
\f[CR]\[rs][\[rs]]\f[R], erasing the right prompt after
submission)[cite: 4].
The terminal window title displays \f[CR]user: directory\f[R] while idle
and the active command while executing[cite: 4].
.PP
