.TE
.SS Command history persistence
Interactive shells with \f[CR]history\f[R] enabled (default) record each
submitted buffer as a single line\-escaped event (\f[CR]\[rs]n\f[R] for
newlines, \f[CR]\[rs]\[rs]\f[R] for backslashes) in
\f[CR]$KOSH_HISTORY_FILE\f[R] (\f[CR]\[ti]/.kosh_history\f[R] default,
mode \f[CR]0600\f[R], directory\-locked during writes)[cite: 4].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Filtering and synchronization\f[R] \- Non\-interactive shells never
record events automatically (only via \f[CR]history \-w\f[R] or
\f[CR]history \-a\f[R])[cite: 4].
Consecutive duplicate events, history expansion errors, and records
exceeding \f[CR]65535\f[R] bytes are skipped[cite: 4].
Interactive shells load the history file at startup and append each
submitted event immediately, without auto\-importing events appended by
concurrent shells (\f[CR]Ctrl\-R\f[R] and \f[CR]history \-S\f[R] read
the shared file snapshot)[cite: 4].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Size bounds\f[R] \- \f[CR]$KOSH_HISTORY_SIZE\f[R] (\f[CR]4096\f[R]
default; \f[CR]0\f[R] disables history) caps both the in\-memory list
and the on\-disk file, which is truncated to the newest
\f[CR]$KOSH_HISTORY_SIZE\f[R] events upon shell exit[cite: 4].
Environment values of \f[CR]KOSH_HISTORY_FILE\f[R] and
\f[CR]KOSH_HISTORY_SIZE\f[R] override
\f[CR]editor.history.file_path\f[R] and
\f[CR]editor.history.max_entries\f[R] from \f[CR]kosh.conf\f[R][cite:
4].
Legacy Bash history variables (\f[CR]HISTFILE\f[R], \f[CR]HISTSIZE\f[R],
etc.)
are ignored[cite: 4].
