\f[CR]KOSH_CALC_HISTORY\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]\[ti]/.kosh_calc_history\f[R]
T}@T{
Interactive expression history file for the \f[CR]calc\f[R]
utility[cite: 4].
T}
T{
\f[CR]KOSH_FLAGS\f[R]
T}@T{
Unset
T}@T{
Default command\-line flags parsed before argv (ignored in secure
setuid/setgid execution; ignores \f[CR]\-c\f[R], \f[CR]\-s\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-format\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-apply\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-as\-language\-server\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-rcfile\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-init\-file\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-\f[R], and operands)[cite: 4].
T}
T{
\f[CR]KOSH_FZF_COMPLETION_COMMAND\f[R],
\f[CR]KOSH_FZF_COMPLETION_OPTS\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]fzf\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-multi \-\-layout=reverse \-\-height=\[ti]40% \-\-min\-height=3\f[R]
T}@T{
External completion selector binary and blank\-split flags[cite: 4].
T}
T{
\f[CR]KOSH_SHELL_INTEGRATION\f[R]
T}@T{
Enabled
T}@T{
Set to \f[CR]0\f[R] to suppress \f[CR]OSC 133\f[R], \f[CR]OSC 7\f[R],
and \f[CR]OSC 633\f[R] terminal marks[cite: 4].
T}
T{
\f[CR]KOSH_WELCOME\f[R], \f[CR]KOSH_FAREWELL\f[R]
T}@T{
Mood\-dependent
T}@T{
Startup and exit banners (\f[CR]Welcome :3\f[R] in \f[CR]kosh\f[R],
\f[CR]Bash me harder!\f[R] in Bash moods, \f[CR]POSIX me harder!\f[R] in
\f[CR]sh\f[R], and \f[CR]Goodbye :c\f[R] on exit)[cite: 4].
Suppress by exporting an empty string or zero\-width string
(\f[CR]printf \-v KOSH_WELCOME \[dq]\[rs]r\[dq]\f[R])[cite: 4].
T}
.TE
.SS Native Koshka builtins
The six native Koshka builtins (\f[CR]assimilate\f[R], \f[CR]bench\f[R],
\f[CR]koshconf\f[R], \f[CR]koshkit\f[R], \f[CR]slurp\f[R], \f[CR]z\f[R])
are available in every mood[cite: 4].
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l.
T{
Builtin and synopsis
T}@T{
Operational specification and exit codes
T}
_
T{
\f[CR]assimilate [options] [TARGET]\f[R]
T}@T{
Deploys the running \f[CR]kosh\f[R] binary locally (when
\f[CR]TARGET\f[R] is omitted) or to a remote host over \f[CR]scp\f[R]
into the first writable \f[CR]PATH\f[R] directory (excluding
\f[CR]sbin\f[R] paths unless \f[CR]\-\-install\-directory=DIR\f[R] is
passed)[cite: 4].
Locally, creates relative symlinks (POSIX) or \f[CR].exe\f[R] hard links
(Windows) for all non\-conflicting bundled utilities and
\f[CR]\-\-link\-mood=MOOD\f[R] (\f[CR]bash\f[R], \f[CR]dash\f[R],
\f[CR]sh\f[R], \f[CR]kosh\f[R]) names, warning once per group of skipped
conflicting names[cite: 4].
Supports \f[CR]\-\-ssh\-command=CMD\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-scp\-command=CMD\f[R], \f[CR]\-x\f[R] (\f[CR]\-\-trace\f[R]),
and \f[CR]\-y\f[R] (\f[CR]\-\-yes\f[R] to skip confirmation)[cite: 4].
Validates the copied binary before atomic replacement and rolls back on
failure[cite: 4].
T}
T{
\f[CR]bench [options] command ...\f[R]
T}@T{
Benchmarks each \f[CR]command\f[R] via \f[CR]kosh \-c\f[R] and reports
mean, standard deviation, and range for wall time, peak RSS, and
platform performance counters[cite: 4].
Stops and returns \f[CR]1\f[R] on nonzero command exit unless
\f[CR]\-\-ignore\-exit\-code\f[R] is set (\f[CR]130\f[R] on
interrupt)[cite: 4].
Options: \f[CR]\-\-show\-output\f[R], \f[CR]\-N\f[R]
(\f[CR]\-\-no\-shell\f[R] direct exec), \f[CR]\-n\f[R]
(\f[CR]\-\-runs\f[R] \f[CR]1\f[R]..\f[CR]100000\f[R]), \f[CR]\-t\f[R]
(\f[CR]\-\-duration\f[R] ms, default \f[CR]3000\f[R]), \f[CR]\-w\f[R]
(\f[CR]\-\-warmup\f[R] \f[CR]1\f[R]..\f[CR]100000\f[R]; without argument
runs 1\-3 warmups until two agree within 10%; default 1 warmup),
\f[CR]\-p\f[R] (\f[CR]\-\-profile\f[R], alias for
\f[CR]\-\-runs 1 \-\-extended\f[R]), and \f[CR]\-E\f[R]
(\f[CR]\-\-extended\f[R] CPU/wait time, context switches, faults, I/O,
plus Linux traced syscalls/threads/execs, macOS energy/wakeups, and
Windows Job Object tree counters)[cite: 4].
T}
T{
\f[CR]koshconf <subcommand> ...\f[R]
T}@T{
Manages configuration settings[cite: 4]:\-
\f[CR]create PRESET [\-\-force]\f[R]: Writes commented \f[CR]kosh\f[R],
\f[CR]bash\f[R], or \f[CR]sh\f[R] preset to user \f[CR]kosh.conf\f[R]
(and default \f[CR]rc.kosh\f[R] if missing)[cite: 4].\-
\f[CR]set OPTION VALUE [\-\-persist]\f[R]: Mutates session option, and
with \f[CR]\-\-persist\f[R] updates user \f[CR]kosh.conf\f[R] (backing
up \f[CR]kosh.conf.bak\f[R])[cite: 4].\- \f[CR]get OPTION\f[R] /
\f[CR]list [\-a|\-\-all]\f[R]: Prints single value or sorted
\f[CR]name=value\f[R] list (\f[CR]\-a\f[R] includes legacy aliases,
\f[CR]hashall\f[R], and \f[CR]nolog\f[R])[cite: 4].\-
\f[CR]load ENCODED\f[R] / \f[CR]save [\-\-persist]\f[R]: Applies or
outputs \f[CR]KOSHCONF\f[R] Base64 payload (\f[CR]save \-\-persist\f[R]
writes non\-default session settings to \f[CR]kosh.conf\f[R])[cite:
4].Returns \f[CR]0\f[R] on success, \f[CR]1\f[R] on invalid option/value
or I/O error, and \f[CR]2\f[R] on syntax error[cite: 4].
Restricted shells reject \f[CR]create\f[R], \f[CR]set\f[R],
\f[CR]load\f[R], and \f[CR]save \-\-persist\f[R][cite: 4].
T}
T{
\f[CR]koshkit [\-\-color when] [utility [arg ...]]\f[R]
T}@T{
Invokes a bundled utility (\f[CR]\-\-color\f[R] takes \f[CR]always\f[R],
\f[CR]never\f[R], or \f[CR]auto\f[R]), or prints the categorized utility
catalog when invoked without arguments (\f[CR]\-\-list\f[R] prints one
utility per line; \f[CR]\-\-list\-flags\f[R] prints utilities and
flags)[cite: 4].
T}
T{
\f[CR]slurp [\-e|\-v|\-V] [+LINE] FILE ...\f[R]
T}@T{
Opens each \f[CR]FILE\f[R] sequentially in the full\-screen
alternate\-buffer editor (\f[CR]\-e\f[R] Emacs mode, \f[CR]\-v\f[R] Vi
insert mode, \f[CR]\-V\f[R] Vi normal mode; \f[CR]+LINE\f[R] jumps to
line)[cite: 4].
Preserves syntax highlighting and \f[CR]:format\f[R] support for shell
scripts, supports mouse positioning/selection/scrolling, and writes
files atomically via sibling temp files (or in\-place with a private
backup in \f[CR]$HOME\f[R] or \f[CR]$TMPDIR\f[R] for multi\-link,
foreign\-owned, or non\-sticky world\-writable directories) while
preserving CRLF endings, final newlines, permissions, and symlinks[cite:
4].
Rejects directories, special/unreadable files, files containing
\f[CR]NUL\f[R] or invalid UTF\-8, files \f[CR]> 16 MiB\f[R], restricted
shells, or non\-tty stdio with status \f[CR]1\f[R] (\f[CR]2\f[R] on
usage errors, \f[CR]130\f[R] on \f[CR]Ctrl\-C\f[R])[cite: 4].
T}
T{
\f[CR]z [query ...]\f[R]
T}@T{
Jumps to a directory recorded in
\f[CR]$KOSH_DIRECTORY_HISTORY\f[R][cite: 4].
A single existing directory path opens directly; multiple operands match
case\-insensitive substrings ranked by visit count and recency; no
operand jumps to \f[CR]$HOME\f[R][cite: 4].
Returns \f[CR]1\f[R] when no match exists[cite: 4].
T}
.TE
.SS Bundled Koshkit utilities
Koshka bundles 108 utilities plus 4 aliases (\f[CR]egrep\f[R] and
\f[CR]fgrep\f[R] for \f[CR]grep\f[R]; \f[CR]vi\f[R] and \f[CR]emacs\f[R]
for \f[CR]slurp \-V\f[R] and \f[CR]slurp \-e\f[R])[cite: 4].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Resolution and invocation\f[R] \- In the \f[CR]kosh\f[R] mood (or
when \f[CR]\-\-enable\-koshkit\f[R] /
\f[CR]interpreter.resolve_koshkit_applets_as_commands=on\f[R] is set),
bundled utilities resolve directly as commands \f[I]after\f[R]
\f[CR]PATH\f[R] lookup[cite: 4].
Invoking the binary via a symlink/hardlink named after a utility
(case\-sensitive, stripping \f[CR].exe\f[R]) or as
\f[CR]koshkit <utility>\f[R] executes the utility directly, bypassing
shell startup files, settings files, and \f[CR]KOSH_FLAGS\f[R][cite: 4].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Option parsing and exit status invariants\f[R] \- Every utility
accepts \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R] (and \f[CR]\-\-version\f[R] when invoked
under its own binary name)[cite: 4].
Flags may appear before or after operands (\f[CR]\-\-\f[R] ends option
parsing), except for command\-wrapping utilities (\f[CR]calc\f[R],
\f[CR]env\f[R], \f[CR]expr\f[R], \f[CR]flock\f[R], \f[CR]nice\f[R],
\f[CR]nohup\f[R], \f[CR]retry\f[R], \f[CR]timeout\f[R],
\f[CR]watch\f[R], \f[CR]xargs\f[R]), which stop parsing options at the
first positional operand[cite: 4].
Utilities return \f[CR]0\f[R] on success, \f[CR]1\f[R] on
operand/processing failure (continuing to remaining file operands), and
\f[CR]2\f[R] on usage errors (which terminates scripts in the
\f[CR]kosh\f[R] mood)[cite: 4].
Interactive prompts (\f[CR]rm \-i\f[R], \f[CR]cp \-i\f[R],
\f[CR]mv \-i\f[R], \f[CR]assimilate\f[R]) print \f[CR][y/N]\f[R] or
\f[CR][Y/n]\f[R] to stderr and read one line from stdin[cite: 4].
.SS Koshka\-specific and system inspection utilities
.PP
