T{
Construct
T}@T{
Syntax and execution semantics across moods
T}
_
T{
Simple commands
T}@T{
\f[CR][var=val ...] [word | redirection ...]\f[R][cite: 4].
All prefix assignment values expand \f[I]before\f[R] any assignment
binds (in \f[CR]a=7 b=$a cmd\f[R], \f[CR]b\f[R] receives the prior value
of \f[CR]a\f[R])[cite: 4].
Prefix assignments on special builtins persist in the shell in
\f[CR]kosh\f[R], \f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R], and \f[CR]sh\f[R], but are
local to the builtin in \f[CR]bash\f[R]; prefix assignments on functions
are temporary in all moods[cite: 4].
Exit status is \f[CR]128 + signo\f[R] if killed by a signal[cite: 4].
T}
T{
Pipelines
T}@T{
\f[CR][time [\-p] [\-R]] [!] cmd1 [ { | | |& } cmd2 ... ]\f[R][cite: 4].
\f[CR]|&\f[R] pipes both stdout and stderr (\f[CR]2>&1 |\f[R])[cite: 4].
In \f[CR]kosh\f[R] and \f[CR]sh\f[R], a builtin in the final pipeline
stage executes in the current shell process (\f[CR]echo 5 | read x\f[R]
sets \f[CR]x\f[R]); in \f[CR]bash\f[R] and \f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R], the
final stage runs in the current shell only when \f[CR]lastpipe=on\f[R]
and job control (\f[CR]monitor\f[R]) is \f[CR]off\f[R][cite: 4].
Empty pipeline stages (\f[CR]p=1 | cat\f[R]) are errors in
\f[CR]kosh\f[R] and no\-op status \f[CR]0\f[R] in compatibility
moods[cite: 4].
Status is the last stage\[aq]s status, or the rightmost failing stage
under \f[CR]pipefail\f[R], negated by \f[CR]!\f[R], with all stage
statuses recorded in \f[CR]PIPESTATUS[\[at]]\f[R][cite: 4].
\f[CR]time\f[R] reports real/user/sys time (plus CPU % and peak RSS in
\f[CR]kosh\f[R] or with \f[CR]\-R\f[R]; \f[CR]\-p\f[R] uses POSIX
format; follows \f[CR]TIMEFORMAT\f[R])[cite: 4].
T}
T{
Lists (\f[CR];\f[R], \f[CR]&\f[R], \f[CR]&&\f[R], \f[CR]||\f[R])
T}@T{
\f[CR]&&\f[R] and \f[CR]||\f[R] share equal left\-associative precedence
and bind tighter than \f[CR];\f[R] and \f[CR]&\f[R][cite: 4].
Trailing \f[CR]&\f[R] runs the entire preceding and\-or list
asynchronously in a background subshell (status \f[CR]0\f[R], PID in
\f[CR]$!\f[R])[cite: 4].
In \f[CR]kosh\f[R], words expand \f[I]before\f[R] spawning a background
simple command; in compatibility moods, expansion occurs inside the
spawned child (failing with \f[CR]127\f[R] or \f[CR]1\f[R] in Bash moods
and \f[CR]2\f[R] in \f[CR]sh\f[R])[cite: 4].
T}
T{
Subshell \f[CR](list)\f[R] & Group \f[CR]{ list; }\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR](list)\f[R] executes in an isolated subshell environment;
\f[CR]{ list; }\f[R] executes in the current shell and requires a
trailing \f[CR];\f[R] or newline before \f[CR]}\f[R][cite: 4].
T}
T{
Arithmetic \f[CR]((expr))\f[R] & Conditional \f[CR][[ expr ]]\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]((expr))\f[R] returns \f[CR]0\f[R] if \f[CR]expr\f[R] evaluates
nonzero, and \f[CR]1\f[R] if zero or empty[cite: 4].
\f[CR][[ expr ]]\f[R] disables word splitting and globbing on operands,
returning \f[CR]0\f[R], \f[CR]1\f[R], or \f[CR]2\f[R] on invalid
syntax[cite: 4].
T}
T{
Loops (\f[CR]for\f[R], \f[CR]select\f[R], \f[CR]while\f[R],
\f[CR]until\f[R])
T}@T{
\f[CR]for name [in word ...]; do list; done\f[R] (requires
\f[CR]do...done\f[R], rejecting \f[CR]{...}\f[R])[cite: 4].
\f[CR]for (( expr1; expr2; expr3 )); do list; done\f[R] treats empty
expressions as \f[CR]1\f[R][cite: 4].
\f[CR]select name [in word ...]; do list; done\f[R]
(\f[CR]bash\f[R]/\f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R] only) prints a numbered menu on
stderr using \f[CR]PS3\f[R] and stores raw input in
\f[CR]REPLY\f[R][cite: 4].
\f[CR]while\f[R] and \f[CR]until\f[R] loop while the condition returns
\f[CR]0\f[R] or nonzero[cite: 4].
T}
T{
Pattern branch \f[CR]case\f[R] & Conditional \f[CR]if\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]case word in [(] pat [| pat]...) list ;;|;&|;;& esac\f[R] where
\f[CR];;\f[R] stops, \f[CR];&\f[R] falls through without testing the
next pattern, and \f[CR];;&\f[R] tests subsequent patterns[cite: 4].
\f[CR]if list; then list; [elif list; then list;]... [else list;] fi\f[R][cite:
4].
T}
T{
Coprocess \f[CR]coproc\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]coproc [NAME] command [redirections]\f[R] (unsupported in
\f[CR]sh\f[R])[cite: 4].
Spawns \f[CR]command\f[R] asynchronously with two pipes (> fd
\f[CR]9\f[R], closed on \f[CR]exec\f[R] and not inherited by subshells),
storing read/write descriptors in \f[CR]NAME[0]\f[R] /
\f[CR]NAME[1]\f[R] (\f[CR]COPROC\f[R] default; \f[CR]NAME\f[R] is
recognized only before a compound command) and PID in
\f[CR]NAME_PID\f[R] and \f[CR]$!\f[R][cite: 4].
T}
T{
Functions \f[CR]fname()\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]fname () command [redirections]\f[R] or
\f[CR]function fname [()] command [redirections]\f[R][cite: 4].
Stores \f[CR]command\f[R] (any simple or compound command) and attaches
redirections to every invocation[cite: 4].
Variables are global unless declared \f[CR]local\f[R]
(\f[CR]local var\f[R] without \f[CR]=val\f[R] inherits the outer value
in \f[CR]kosh\f[R] and \f[CR]sh\f[R], and starts unset in Bash
moods)[cite: 4].
Nesting caps at \f[CR]900\f[R] function calls and \f[CR]400\f[R] sourced
files[cite: 4].
T}
.TE
.SS Parameters, variables, and arrays
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Assignment evaluation\f[R] \- \f[CR]name=value\f[R] and
\f[CR]name+=value\f[R] undergo tilde expansion (after \f[CR]=\f[R] and
after any \f[CR]:\f[R]), parameter/command/arithmetic expansion, and
quote removal, without word splitting or globbing[cite: 4].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Special parameters\f[R]:
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]$*\f[R] and \f[CR]$\[at]\f[R]: Positional parameters from
\f[CR]$1\f[R][cite: 4].
Unquoted, both split on \f[CR]IFS\f[R][cite: 4].
\f[CR]\[dq]$*\[dq]\f[R] joins with the first byte of \f[CR]IFS\f[R];
\f[CR]\[dq]$\[at]\[dq]\f[R] expands to separate words[cite: 4].
When joined into a single scalar (such as \f[CR]v=$\[at]\f[R]),
\f[CR]$\[at]\f[R] joins with the first byte of \f[CR]IFS\f[R] in
\f[CR]sh\f[R] and with a space in Bash/\f[CR]kosh\f[R] moods[cite: 4].
In the \f[CR]sh\f[R] mood, \f[CR]$\[at]\f[R] and \f[CR]$*\f[R] are
always treated as set inside \f[CR]${\[at]\-d}\f[R] and
\f[CR]${\[at]+p}\f[R][cite: 4].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]$#\f[R] (parameter count), \f[CR]$?\f[R] (last foreground exit
status), \f[CR]$\-\f[R] (active option flags, including \f[CR]h\f[R] and
\f[CR]B\f[R] by default, \f[CR]c\f[R] for \f[CR]\-c\f[R], and
\f[CR]u\f[R] in \f[CR]kosh\f[R]), \f[CR]$$\f[R] (shell PID, preserved in
subshells), \f[CR]$!\f[R] (last background/coproc/process\-substitution
PID), \f[CR]$0\f[R] (shell/script name), and \f[CR]$_\f[R] (final
argument of previous simple command)[cite: 4].
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Indexed and associative arrays\f[R] \- Indexed arrays
(\f[CR]a=(x y)\f[R], \f[CR]a=([2]=c)\f[R], \f[CR]a[i]=v\f[R],
\f[CR]a+=(w)\f[R]) support sparse non\-contiguous integer subscripts
(\f[CR]${a[i]}\f[R], where negative indices count from the end, and
scalar \f[CR]$a\f[R] is \f[CR]${a[0]}\f[R])[cite: 4].
Associative arrays (\f[CR]declare \-A m\f[R], \f[CR]m[key]=v\f[R])
preserve insertion order when listing keys via
\f[CR]${!m[\[at]]}\f[R][cite: 4].
Under \f[CR]set \-u\f[R], \f[CR]${a[\[at]]}\f[R] and \f[CR]${a[*]}\f[R]
on an unset array expand cleanly to nothing, whereas \f[CR]$a\f[R] and
\f[CR]${a[0]}\f[R] trigger an unbound variable error[cite: 4].
Exporting an array (\f[CR]export a\f[R] / \f[CR]declare \-x a\f[R])
records the \f[CR]\-x\f[R] attribute in \f[CR]declare \-p\f[R] without
passing the array into child process environments[cite: 4].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Shell\-maintained and configuration variables\f[R] \- Beyond the
Koshka variables in Koshka variables, Koshka maintains \f[CR]BASH\f[R],
\f[CR]BASH_VERSION\f[R] (\f[CR]5.3.0(1)\-kosh\f[R]),
\f[CR]BASH_VERSINFO\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_ALIASES\f[R],
\f[CR]BASH_ARGC\f[R]/\f[CR]BASH_ARGV\f[R] (populated under
\f[CR]extdebug\f[R]), \f[CR]BASH_ARGV0\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_COMMAND\f[R],
\f[CR]BASH_EXECUTION_STRING\f[R],
\f[CR]BASH_LINENO\f[R]/\f[CR]BASH_SOURCE\f[R]/\f[CR]FUNCNAME\f[R] (empty
in \f[CR]sh\f[R]), \f[CR]BASH_MONOSECONDS\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_REMATCH\f[R],
\f[CR]BASH_SUBSHELL\f[R], \f[CR]BASHOPTS\f[R], \f[CR]BASHPID\f[R],
\f[CR]COMP_*\f[R], \f[CR]COPROC\f[R]/\f[CR]COPROC_PID\f[R],
\f[CR]DIRSTACK\f[R], \f[CR]EPOCHREALTIME\f[R]/\f[CR]EPOCHSECONDS\f[R],
\f[CR]EUID\f[R]/\f[CR]UID\f[R], \f[CR]GROUPS\f[R], \f[CR]HISTCMD\f[R],
\f[CR]HOSTNAME\f[R]/\f[CR]HOSTTYPE\f[R]/\f[CR]MACHTYPE\f[R]/\f[CR]OSTYPE\f[R],
\f[CR]LINENO\f[R], \f[CR]MAPFILE\f[R], \f[CR]OLDPWD\f[R]/\f[CR]PWD\f[R],
\f[CR]OPTARG\f[R]/\f[CR]OPTIND\f[R], \f[CR]PIPESTATUS\f[R],
\f[CR]PPID\f[R] (read\-only except in \f[CR]sh\f[R]), \f[CR]RANDOM\f[R],
\f[CR]REPLY\f[R], \f[CR]SECONDS\f[R], \f[CR]SHELLOPTS\f[R],
\f[CR]SHLVL\f[R] (resets to \f[CR]1\f[R] if negative or
\f[CR]>= 1000\f[R]), and \f[CR]SRANDOM\f[R], and honors
\f[CR]BASH_COMPLETION_VERSINFO\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_ENV\f[R]/\f[CR]ENV\f[R],
\f[CR]BASH_XTRACEFD\f[R], \f[CR]CDPATH\f[R],
\f[CR]COLUMNS\f[R]/\f[CR]LINES\f[R],
\f[CR]FCEDIT\f[R]/\f[CR]EDITOR\f[R]/\f[CR]VISUAL\f[R],
\f[CR]GLOBIGNORE\f[R], \f[CR]HOME\f[R], \f[CR]IFS\f[R],
\f[CR]IGNOREEOF\f[R], \f[CR]LANG\f[R]/\f[CR]LC_*\f[R],
\f[CR]MANPATH\f[R], \f[CR]NO_COLOR\f[R], \f[CR]OPTERR\f[R],
\f[CR]PATH\f[R],
\f[CR]PROMPT_COMMAND\f[R]/\f[CR]PS0\f[R]..\f[CR]PS4\f[R]/\f[CR]RPS1\f[R]/\f[CR]RPROMPT\f[R],
\f[CR]SHELL\f[R],
\f[CR]TERM\f[R]/\f[CR]COLORTERM\f[R]/\f[CR]TERM_PROGRAM\f[R],
